Linux-port render parity (development record #407): phy: rockchip: inno-dsidphy: RK3128 LVDS sample clock and VOCM as u-boot.

Two LVDS PHY settings of the RK3128 path differed from the state the board's u-boot leaves and
Android runs with (the vendor 3.10 kernel never runs its LVDS init while u-boot's picture is up:
rk312x_lcdc_open() skips trsm_ops->enable() under support_uboot_display()):

- analog register 0x08 bit 4, the sample clock direction: the 4.4 BSP flow (and mainline's)
  sets it to reverse; the 3.10 driver never writes the register and u-boot leaves it forward
  (0x4c; ours read 0x5c). The RK3128's VOP inverts the LVDS dclk instead (patch 407-0001).
- LVDS register 0x04, VOCM (bits 5:4): u-boot leaves 2 (0xaa), #292's patch 0002 wrote the 3.10
  driver's 0 (0x8a). DIFF_V (bits 7:6) is 2 in both.

Keep the forward sample clock and VOCM 2 for rockchip,rk3128-dsi-dphy (lvds_analog_init); the
other SoCs keep the reverse direction.

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
@@ -611,19 +611,24 @@
 	u16 fbdiv = 28;
 
 	if (inno->pdata->lvds_analog_init) {
-		/* Common-mode voltage 900 mV, differential swing 350 mV */
+		/* Common-mode voltage and differential swing as u-boot sets them */
 		phy_update_bits(inno, REGISTER_PART_LVDS, 0x04,
 				LVDS_VOCM_MASK | LVDS_DIFF_V_MASK,
-				LVDS_VOCM(0) | LVDS_DIFF_V(2));
+				LVDS_VOCM(2) | LVDS_DIFF_V(2));
 		/* The MSB of each pixel component is on D7 */
 		phy_update_bits(inno, REGISTER_PART_LVDS, 0x00,
 				LVDS_MSB_SEL_MASK, LVDS_MSB_SEL_D7);
 	}
 
-	/* Sample clock reverse direction */
+	/*
+	 * Sample clock reverse direction; the RK3128 keeps the forward one its
+	 * u-boot leaves (the VOP inverts the LVDS dclk there instead).
+	 */
 	phy_update_bits(inno, REGISTER_PART_ANALOG, 0x08,
 			SAMPLE_CLOCK_DIRECTION_MASK | LOWFRE_EN_MASK,
-			SAMPLE_CLOCK_DIRECTION_REVERSE |
+			(inno->pdata->lvds_analog_init ?
+			 SAMPLE_CLOCK_DIRECTION_FORWARD :
+			 SAMPLE_CLOCK_DIRECTION_REVERSE) |
 			PLL_OUTPUT_FREQUENCY_DIV_BY_1);
 
 	/* Select LVDS mode */
